{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeseJZeQjZ87WNcScdrHU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` — Shipment data class with status field\n- `Shipment.kt:23-27` — ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-22` — save(), findById(), existsById() methods\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-55` — Existing POST create and GET endpoints\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` — Exception handler that wraps ApiException into ApiError response\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Test patterns using MockMvc and jsonPath assertions\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Error handling uses custom ApiException subclasses that encode HTTP status\n2. All errors wrapped in ApiError envelope with code and message\n3. Tests use MockMvc with POST/GET builders and jsonPath assertions\n4. Endpoints return 201 for creation (CREATED status), 200 for GET, 404 for not found, 409 for conflict\n5. Services fetch by ID and throw ResourceNotFoundException if missing before proceeding\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Must add ErrorCode for shipment in wrong status (409 case)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Must add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Must add tests covering all four cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotency requirement: confirming already-CONFIRMED shipment must succeed, not fail\n- Must distinguish between 200 (OK) and 409 (Conflict) responses\n\n**Open questions:** None; requirement clearly specifies all cases.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the ErrorCode enum. This covers the case where a shipment cannot be confirmed because it's in CANCELLED state.\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`**: Add a new method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` decorated with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`. The method will:\n   - Fetch the shipment by ID, throwing `ResourceNotFoundException` if missing (404)\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return HTTP 200 with the unchanged shipment (idempotent)\n   - If status is CREATED, update it to CONFIRMED, persist it, return HTTP 200 with updated shipment\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` (409)\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`**: Add four test cases:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment transitions to CONFIRMED and returns 200\n   - Confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds and returns 200 (idempotence)\n   - Confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS error code\n   - Confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- *Create a service layer*: The ticket says \"Do not modify files outside the shipment feature except tests\" and existing endpoints are in the controller. A new service would violate the spirit of minimalism. Controller logic is acceptable here since operations are simple.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|-------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | shipmentId | findById | save(updated) | 200 + Shipment | return ResponseEntity.ok(saved) |\n| CONFIRMED idempotent | shipmentId | findById | none | 200 + Shipment | return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) |\n| CANCELLED conflict | shipmentId | findById | none | 409 + ApiError | throw ConflictException |\n| Not found | shipmentId | findById returns null | none | 404 + ApiError | throw ResourceNotFoundException |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. Test: `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED status` — Create S-1, POST confirm, expect 200, verify status is CONFIRMED in response\n2. Test: `confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds idempotently` — Create S-2, POST confirm twice, both return 200, no error\n3. Test: `rejects confirmation of a CANCELLED shipment with 409` — Directly save CANCELLED shipment to repo, POST confirm, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS code\n4. Test: `reports an unknown shipment as 404` — POST confirm on non-existent ID, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\n**Add ErrorCode for shipment status conflict:**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1214,"cache_read_input_tokens":16457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1214},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e38fffbf-c91b-43e1-b11e-4fa6a9db3c51","uuid":"d8641e4f-d371-4a30-9f41-beaaf8e58a0b","timestamp":"2026-09-09T09:40:07.122Z","request_id":"req_011CeseJYq3k3K23APFNV7rY"}
